(5999835, 863415, 43463, '<td valign="top">This is a very artsy interesting composition - a cross between Monet and Magritte. Monet''s watercolor paintings of flowers observed/appreciated by an faceless lady with lively and vivid orange hair. She is faceless because she could be anyone - a way for some observers to place themselves in her shoes - As she observes the painting and contemplates what she sees so to do we observe the ''art'' photo of her and we now slip into the same shoes of observing and comtemplating the piece. The orange hair and the collar are bold and vibrant which may be a statement about the personality of the lady we are observing.</td>', 'This is a very artsy interesting composition - a cross between Monet and Magritte. Monet''s watercolor paintings of flowers observed/appreciated by an faceless lady with lively and vivid orange hair. She is faceless because she could be anyone - a way for some observers to place themselves in her shoes - As she observes the painting and contemplates what she sees so to do we observe the ''art'' photo of her and we now slip into the same shoes of observing and comtemplating the piece. The orange hair and the collar are bold and vibrant which may be a statement about the personality of the lady we are observing.', '2010-05-10 09:39:06.000000', NULL, 0),
